<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexios III of Trebizond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1338–1390</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Alexios III Megas Komnenos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexios III Megas Komnenos was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> from 1349 to 1390. He restored order after years of civil war and kept the small empire safe by diplomacy, marrying his daughters to neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a>, including Taceddin. He founded churches and endowed the Dionysiou monastery on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a>, and Sumela monastery prospered under his patronage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-of-trebizond.jpg" alt="Alexios III of Trebizond" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Bender235 at German Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexios3_komnenos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
